Options:

  => -f: This is a test operator that returns true if the specified path exists and is a regular file.

  => -d: checks if a directory exists

  => -e: checks if any file or directory exists

  => -s: checks if a file exists and is not empty.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Script to check the file availability:

#!/bin/bash

read -p "Enter the file name (including the path): " file_name

if [ -f $file_name ]; then
	echo "File found."
else
	echo "File not found. Creating the file at mentioned location"
	$(touch $file_name)
fi

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Script to check the availability of a directory:

#!/bin/bash

read -p "Enter the directory name: " dir_name

if [ -d $dir_name ]; then
    echo "Directory found."
else
    echo "Directory not found."
fi
